use std
into dial.amni
lang amni

Amni Dial: a GPU coding console that drives four coding-agent CLIs, one wheel sector per session, with a shader-rendered black hole that swallows old output. Imports os, gfx, math, json, `gfx.codec_png`, `gfx.sdf_font` (`sdf_text`, `sdf_text_w`, `sdf_rect`, `sdf_draw`, `TextVtx` with pos, uv, col). Use these std calls and no others for the same jobs (never `extern` and never a hand-written JSON parser): `run_command(cmd)` returns the shell exit status; `is_dir(path)`, `file_exists(path)`; `read_file(path, out)` returns false when missing; `write_file(path, text)`, `append_file(path, text)`; `env(name, out)` returns false when unset; `args()`; `sleep_ms(ms)`; `split(text, byte)`; `str(...)` joins text and numbers; `copy`; `print`. JSON: one reused `json::Doc {}`; `let root, msg = json::parse(text, doc)` gives a negative root on failure; `json::member(doc, node, key)`, `json::element(doc, node, k)`, `json::count(doc, node)`, `json::kind(doc, node)` compared with `json::K_STR`, `json::text_of(doc, node)`, `let v, ok = json::as_f64(doc, node)`, `let b, ok = json::as_bool(doc, node)`, `json::format_string(out, text)`; a missing member is a negative node. Text is a growable byte list (empty is `[]`); a session's lines are a list of them; colors are 4-byte arrays like `TextVtx.col`. Floats are f32 unless stated; NOW, T0 and the spin duration are real. Platforms p from 0 to 3, in this order: name "Grok Bot", "Claude Code", "Antigravity", "OpenCode"; key "grok", "claude", "antigravity", "opencode"; executable "grok", "claude", "agy", "opencode". ENVP is the shell prefix `PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$HOME/.opencode/bin:$HOME/.agy/bin:$HOME/.grok/bin:$PATH"; ` (ending in a space). RAD = 0.017453292, SPIN = 0.7 seconds.

A session holds its platform, number n, directory, session id text, working directory text, model text, display lines, a last-seen size (start -1), a shown-line count, busy flag, busy start time (real, -1 when unknown) and demo flag. Module state: sessions list S, availability per platform AV, last-visited session per platform LASTP, ROOT, HOME text, CUR, ROT, ROT0, ROT1 (all 0), T0 = -9, NOW, SCROLL, VIEW, HIDE, INPUT text, DARK true, FRAMES false, W = 1400, H = 900, CX = 700, CY = 450, R = 400, WRAPU = 40, YS = 1, BX, BY, WG = 0, S0 = 27, FR = 0, font metrics FY0 = 0, FY1 = 1 and FC = 0.5, LOGO (a vertex list built once at startup), GPU state READY false, four pipelines PB, PO, PD, PU, a sampler SM, a scene texture SC, four bloom textures BL, their size TW = 0 and TH = 0, and up to two holes HX (each four floats x, y, radius, alpha) with count NH. Two uniform structs: `HoleU` with four 4-float vectors a, h0, h1, m and `PostU` with two 4-float vectors a, b.

Colors. A float 0 to 1 becomes a byte as `clamp(x*255, 0, 255)` cut to int. rgba(c, a) packs c's three channels and a. Theme color k with alpha a, dark then light: k0 (0.012,0.018,0.04) / (0.958,0.938,0.882); k1 (0.90,0.88,0.82) / (0.20,0.16,0.09); k2 (1.0,0.80,0.42) / (0.70,0.50,0.12); k3 (0.55,0.58,0.68) / (0.48,0.42,0.32); k4 (0.03,0.045,0.09) / (0.995,0.98,0.94); otherwise (0,0,0) / (0.80,0.68,0.42). Accent color k with alpha a, dark then light: k0 code (0.55,0.90,0.95) / (0.10,0.42,0.50); k1 tool (0.47,0.80,0.98) / (0.17,0.38,0.62); k2 error (1.0,0.40,0.33) / (0.75,0.17,0.12); k3 live (0.40,0.95,0.55) / (0.15,0.55,0.25); k4 busy (1.0,0.72,0.25) / (0.78,0.47,0.05); otherwise demo (0.72,0.55,1.0) / (0.45,0.30,0.75). Platform color: p0 (0.55,0.57,0.65), p1 (0.85,0.50,0.32), p2 (0.32,0.55,0.95), p3 (0.40,0.75,0.45). Shadow color for alpha a: theme 5 with alpha a times 0.45 when dark, 0.12 when light.

Sessions. A session's directory is "ROOT/key/n". Adding one appends it with demo set when "dir/demo" exists, empty cwd and model, busy start -1, and returns its index. Making one for p takes the lowest n from 1 whose directory does not exist, runs `mkdir -p '<dir>'` and adds it. Scanning: for each platform add every existing n from 1 while its directory exists, making one if none existed; then LASTP[p] is the first session index of p (or -1). A platform is available when `command -v <exe> >/dev/null 2>&1`, prefixed by ENVP, exits 0. Tilde form of a path: when it starts with HOME, "~" followed by the rest, else the path.

Navigation. rank(i) counts earlier sessions of i's platform; nth(p, r) is the index of p's session of rank r (or -1); cnt(p) counts p's sessions. Span is 360 / session count degrees; order(i) is rank(i) plus the sessions of a lower platform; a session's center is (order + 0.5) * span. ang(t) = (t + ROT + 90) * RAD. Wrapping an angle in degrees subtracts 360 while above 180 and adds 360 while below -180. Going to session i: d = wrap(-center(i) - ROT1); ROT0 = ROT; ROT1 becomes ROT1 + d; T0 = NOW; CUR = i; LASTP of its platform = i; VIEW = 0; its shown count = visible(i). Visible lines are max(0, lines - HIDE) for CUR, else all lines. Stepping by dir goes to nth(p, (rank(CUR) + dir + m) % m) for CUR's platform p with m sessions of it.

Display lines. Every line's first byte is its kind letter: "u" user prompt, "t" tool call, "e" error, "c" code, "h" heading, "r" horizontal rule, "b" table row, "H" table header row, "m" meta, "q" quote, "p" plain. A line holding only "p" is a blank line. After the kind letter comes the display text, where byte 1 toggles an inline code span, byte 2 toggles a bold span and, in table rows, byte 9 separates cells. The visible width of text at size s sums `sdf_text_w` at size s of each run between marker bytes 1, 2 and 9, ignoring the markers.

Wrapping `wrap(out, k, t)` appends the display text t as one or more lines of kind k. Walk t by UTF-8 lead byte (at least 240 is 4 bytes, 224 is 3, 192 is 2, else 1), taking the clipped bytes as the character. Skip "\r", 4-byte characters and stray continuation bytes (128 to 191). A tab becomes two spaces, except byte 9 in kinds "b" and "H", which is kept. Bytes 1, 2 and 9 are kept without adding width. The current line starts as the kind letter; after each other character add its `sdf_text_w` at size 1 to the width. In kinds "b", "H" and "t", once the width exceeds WRAPU, append "…" and ignore the rest of t. Otherwise, when the width exceeds WRAPU, find the last space after position 1 searching back from the end, cut there if that position exceeds len/3 (integer) else at the full length, push the part before the cut, and start the next line with the kind letter, then byte 1 if an odd number of byte 1 sits in the pushed part, then byte 2 if an odd number of byte 2 sits in it, then the part after the cut skipping one byte; the width becomes the visible width of that remainder at size 1. At the end push the current line when it holds more than the kind letter.

Inline marks of a text line: copy it, turning each "`" into byte 1 and each "**" into byte 2; every other byte stays.

`emit(out, t, base)` adds a whole message t with base kind letter base. Split t on newlines into source lines, with a code flag starting off. For each source line s with leading and trailing spaces trimmed into ts: when the code flag is on, a ts starting with "```" turns it off, else wrap s as kind "c" with no inline marks. Otherwise a ts starting with "```" turns the code flag on. Otherwise when base is not "p": wrap the inline-marked s as kind base. Otherwise: an empty ts pushes "p" unless out is empty or out's last line is just "p"; one to six "#" followed by a space make kind "h" from the text after that space; a ts of three or more characters, all "-", all "*" or all "_", pushes "r"; a ts starting with "|" whose bytes are all among "|", "-", ":" and space changes out's last line kind byte from "b" to "H" when it is "b" and pushes nothing; any other ts starting with "|" splits ts on "|", drops the first piece and the last piece when empty, trims each piece, inline-marks each and joins them with byte 9 as kind "b"; leading spaces n then "- ", "* " or "+ " make kind "p" from n spaces, "• " and the rest; "> " makes kind "q" from the rest; anything else is kind "p" from the inline-marked s.

Fixed decimals of a non-negative real v with d decimals: round v times 10 to the d to an integer, write the integer part, then "." and the remainder zero-padded to d digits (no point when d is 0). Tool summary of a JSON node: the first non-empty string member among "file_path", "command", "pattern", "path", "url", "query", "description", "prompt", cut at its first newline, in tilde form, and when longer than 90 bytes cut to 87 bytes (backing up past continuation bytes 128 to 191) plus "…".

Event parsing takes one JSON object node n and the session index i. A string member reads as its text, else "". The id is the first non-empty of "session_id", "sessionID", "conversation_id"; when non-empty it replaces the session id. With type t: "user" with non-empty "text" pushes "p" then emits text as base "u", then stops. "user" with a "message" member: for each element of its "content" with "type" "tool_result" and "is_error" true, the error text is its "content" when a string, else the "text" of the content's first element; emit "Tool failed: " plus its first line as base "e"; then stop. "system": when "cwd" is non-empty store it as the session cwd, when "model" is non-empty store it as the session model; stop. "assistant" with a "message" member: for each element of its "content", type "text" emits its "text" as base "p", type "tool_use" emits byte 2, its "name", byte 2, two spaces and the tool summary of its "input" member as base "t"; stop. With a "part" member: type "text" emits its text as base "p", type "tool" emits byte 2, its "tool", byte 2, two spaces and the tool summary of the part's "state" member's "input" member as base "t"; stop. "result": when "is_error" is true and "result" is non-empty emit "result" as base "e"; then build pieces: "done in " plus fixed 1 decimal of "duration_ms" over 1000 plus " s" when that number exists, "$" plus fixed 4 decimals of "total_cost_usd" when it exists, "num_turns" plus " turns" when it exists; join with "  ·  " and emit as base "m" when any; stop. Types "stream_event", "step_start", "step_finish" stop. Error message: when "error" is a string, that string; else error's "message" if non-empty, else error's "data" "message". Non-empty emits it as base "e" and stops. Otherwise emit the first non-empty of "response", "text", "output" as base "p" if any.

Refreshing session i: busy is whether "dir/busy" exists; when busy and the busy start is negative set it to NOW, when not busy set it to -1. Read "dir/log.jsonl" and "dir/err.log" (missing reads as empty); when log length + 7 * err length equals the stored size do nothing, else store it. Split the log on newlines; a line starting with "{" clears the accumulator; append the line and a newline; parse the accumulator into one reused Doc, and on success clear it and parse the event. Then if err is non-empty and not busy, emit each non-empty line among the last three of err split on newlines as base "e". Replace the session's lines and id.

The command for session i in dir d, with rs = flag + id when the id is non-empty (flags " --session ", " --resume ", " --conversation ", " -s " by platform), else empty:
- p1: "claude -p --output-format stream-json --verbose --permission-mode acceptEdits" rs " < 'd/prompt.txt'"
- p2: "agy --print \"$(cat 'd/prompt.txt')\" --output-format json" rs
- p3: "opencode run --format json ${AMNI_DIAL_OPENCODE_MODEL:+-m $AMNI_DIAL_OPENCODE_MODEL}" rs " < 'd/prompt.txt'"
- p0: "grok --prompt-file 'd/prompt.txt' --output-format streaming-messages-json --permission-mode dontAsk" (no rs)

Sending does nothing when INPUT is empty or CUR's platform is unavailable, busy or demo. Otherwise write INPUT to "d/prompt.txt"; append `{"type":"user","text":` + JSON string of INPUT + "}\n" to the log; write "1" to "d/busy", mark busy and set busy start to NOW; write "d/run.sh" as ENVP + command + " >> 'd/log.jsonl' 2>> 'd/err.log'; rm -f 'd/busy'\n"; run `if command -v setsid >/dev/null; then setsid -f sh 'd/run.sh'; else (sh 'd/run.sh' &); fi >/dev/null 2>&1 </dev/null`; clear INPUT, VIEW = 0, refresh CUR.

Seeding from path: if the file cannot be read print "no transcript " + path and stop. For the first Claude session write its log as `{"type":"user","text":"Make one focused improvement to helium-graphics."}` newline `{"type":"replay","text":` + JSON string of the file + "}\n", write "recorded Claude Code run, replayed" to its "demo" file, set demo and size -1.

Drawing primitives append untextured vertices (uv (-1,-1)). A quad p0 p1 p2 p3 with colors c0 c1 c2 c3 is the triangles p0 p1 p2 and p0 p2 p3 with matching colors; a flat quad uses one color. pt(r, a) = (CX + r*cos(a), CY + r*sin(a)*YS). A band from radius r0 to r1 over angles a0 to a1 with inner color ci and outer color co uses n = max(1, int(|a1-a0|/0.02) + 1) quads with u_k = a0 + (a1-a0)*k/n, corners pt(r0,u0), pt(r1,u0), pt(r1,u1), pt(r0,u1) colored ci, co, co, ci; a one-color band passes the color twice. A disc temporarily moves the center to (x, y) and draws a one-color band 0 to r over 0 to 6.2832. A segment from p to q of width w offsets by n = the unit normal of q - p times w*0.5 and draws the flat quad p-n, q-n, q+n, p+n. A spoke at angle a, radii r0 to r1, width w is the segment from pt(r0,a) to pt(r1,a).

Font metrics, once at startup: lay out "Hgjy|" into a scratch list with `sdf_text(list, 0, 0, 100, "Hgjy|", white, 0, false)` (eight arguments, the last is the outline flag); FY0 is the smallest vertex y over 100 and FY1 the largest over 100. FC is the middle of the smallest and largest vertex y of "H" laid out alone the same way into a second scratch list, over 100 (the capital-letter center). Line height at size s is (FY1 - FY0) * s * 1.12.

Rich text `rich(vs, x, y, size, t, c, weight, cw, draw)` lays out display text t (no kind letter) left to right from pen x and returns the pen advance. Runs between marker bytes are laid out with `sdf_text(vs, pen, y, size, run, color, weight, false)` (eight arguments, the last is the outline flag) when draw is set, and the pen grows by `sdf_text_w` of the run. Byte 1 toggles code style: color is accent 0 with c's alpha. Byte 2 toggles bold: weight 1 and the color mixed 35% toward white when dark or toward black when light, alpha kept. Byte 9 moves the pen to x + cw times the cell index so far. Vertices that `sdf_text` emits with zero RGB get the shadow color for c's alpha over 255.

Arc text `arctext(vs, t, r, a, size, c, weight, tilt, center, cw)` returns an end angle. Lay out t with rich at origin, drawing. fl is sin(a) above 0.25; w is the returned advance; hw = w*0.5/r; start a0 is a+hw when fl and centered, a-hw when only centered, else a. Each new vertex p maps to q = pt(r - (FY1*size - p.y)*tilt, a0 - p.x/r) when fl, else pt(r - (p.y - FY0*size)*tilt, a0 + p.x/r). When WG is above 0, with d = q - (BX,BY): sw = WG*WG*1.5*(1 + 45/(sqrt(dx*dx+dy*dy)+30)), pl = 1 - pow(WG,1.1)*0.97, position = (BX + (dx*cos(sw) - dy*sin(sw))*pl, BY + (dx*sin(sw) + dy*cos(sw))*pl*(1 - WG*0.5)). The end angle is a0 - w/r when fl, else a0 + w/r. `arc_mid(m, a, size)` is the radius at which arc text at angle a and that size centers its capital letters on radius m: m + (FY1 - FC)*size when sin(a) is above 0.25, else m + (FC - FY0)*size. Flat text `flat(vs, x, y, size, t, c, weight)` is rich at (x, y) with cw 0, drawing, returning the advance.

Logo, once at startup: PNG-decode the embedded "amniscient-logo.png" (skip on failure), ch = bytes/(w*h). Over a 112 grid, each cell averages 4 samples k at pixel offset ((y*h/112 + k%2*4)*w + x*w/112 + k/2*4)*ch: s grows by c*0.25 and lo by (1 - min(r,g,b))*0.25. Alpha = clamp(lo*2.2, 0, 1); skip below 0.05; add a quad of color rgba(s, alpha) from (x/112*2-1, y/112*2-1) with side 2/112.

Status of session i: demo gives "DEMO REPLAY  ·  recorded Claude Code run"; unavailable gives "no public Grok Bot API  ·  install the grok CLI to drive this sector" for p0, else exe + " not installed  ·  adapter ready"; busy gives "working  ·  " + int(NOW - busy start) + " s" when the busy start is not negative, else "working"; else "live  ·  Enter sends". Its tone is accent 5 for demo, 2 unavailable, 4 busy, else 3.

Geometry per draw: a = span*0.5*RAD; S0 = clamp(H*0.024, 13, 27); R = H*1.3 + W*0.5/sin(a); CX = W*0.5; CY = H*0.935 - R. w = W*0.78/S0; when |w - WRAPU| exceeds 0.5, set WRAPU = w and reset size to -1 and refresh every session. Text size at radius r is S0*exp(-(R-r)/(H*1.7)). The hole depth is H*0.78 and the hole radius H*0.047.

GPU setup `gpu()`: the first time, PB = a pipeline of embedded shaders "shaders/screen.vert" and "shaders/hole.frag" with the default description; PO the same shaders with blend `gfx::BLEND_PREMULTIPLIED`; PD = "shaders/screen.vert" with "shaders/post.frag" default; PU the same with blend `gfx::BLEND_ADD`; SM = a linear clamped sampler; READY true. Then when TW differs from W or TH from H: release SC and the four BL textures if TW is above 0, make SC a W by H `gfx::RGBA16F` render target and BL[k] a max(1, W >> (k+1)) by max(1, H >> (k+1)) RGBA16F render target, set TW = W, TH = H.

A hole pass with mode m (0 backdrop, 1 overlay) opens a render pass with `gfx::begin_pass(gfx::PassDesc { color: [SC, gfx::Texture { 0 }, gfx::Texture { 0 }, gfx::Texture { 0 }], clear_color: c, .. })` where c is whether the mode is 0 (the field is `clear_color`; cleared passes clear to black), binds PB for mode 0 or PO for mode 1, sets fragment uniforms slot 0 to `HoleU` with a = (W, H, NOW modulo 1000, 0 when DARK else 1), h0 and h1 the first and second holes (zeros when absent), m = (mode, 0.27, 1, 0), draws 3 vertices and ends the pass. A post pass into dst from src and glo with mode m, strength k and add flag opens the same kind of pass on dst with `clear_color` set unless add, binds PU when add else PD, binds fragment textures slot 0 src and slot 1 glo with SM, sets fragment uniforms slot 0 to `PostU` with a = (1/src width, 1/src height, m, k) and b = (NOW modulo 1000, 0.78, 0.022 when DARK else 0, 0 when DARK else 1), draws 3 vertices and ends the pass. Texture sizes come from `gfx::texture_info`.

Adding a hole (x, y, radius, alpha): when NH is below 2 store it and count it; otherwise replace the stored hole of lower alpha when alpha is higher.

Crawl for session i at angle c with alpha a writes lines into va and the prompt into vb. hh = H; r0 = R - S0*1.75; n = visible(i); me is 1 for CUR else 0; the hole center is pt(R - hh*0.78, c) into BX, BY, added as a hole with radius hh*0.047 and alpha a. rr = r0 - S0*2.3 + SCROLL*line height(S0)*me. bw is WRAPU*S0*0.5. For k from 0 while k is below 240 and the line index n-1-VIEW*me-k is at least 0: l is that line, kd its kind letter, x its text after the kind byte. f = (R-rr)/(hh*0.78), stop if above 1. size = size(rr) times 1.12 for "h", 0.87 for "m", else 1. WG = clamp((f-0.58)/0.42, 0, 1); fade = a*(1 - WG*WG*WG)*clamp((r0 - S0*1.47 - rr)/(S0*0.83), 0, 1). Color: "u" theme 2, "t" accent 1, "e" accent 2, "c" accent 0, "h" theme 2, "H" theme 2, "m" theme 3 times 0.8 alpha, "q" theme 3, else theme 1, all with alpha fade; then mix its RGB toward ember (1.0,0.42,0.18) dark or (0.55,0.2,0.1) light by WG*0.8. Weight 1 for "u", "h", "H", else 0. tilt = 0.75+0.25*(1-f). The bands drawn in the crawl (rule, code plate, accent bar, header underline) use alpha times (1 - WG) cubed on top of fade, since only text is pulled into the hole. When fade exceeds 0.01: "r" draws a one-color band rr - size*0.5 to rr - size*0.43 over c ± bw*size/S0*0.8/rr in theme 2 alpha fade*0.35; code and tables keep fixed angles taken at r0 (not rr), so their left edges form one continuous straight edge and indentation and columns line up: "c" with ce = (bw + S0*0.7)/r0 first draws a one-color band rr - line height(size) to rr (consecutive code lines tile with no overlap) over c - ce to c + ce in (0.07,0.09,0.14) alpha fade*0.85 when dark or (0.9,0.87,0.8) alpha fade*0.85 when light, then an accent bar band over the same radii from c + ce - 3/r0 to c + ce in accent 0 alpha fade*0.8, then left-aligned arc text of x at c + bw/r0; "b" and "H" are left-aligned arc text of x at c + bw*0.9/r0 with cw = WRAPU*S0*0.9 over (count of byte 9 in x plus 1), and "H" adds a one-color band rr + size*0.12 to rr + size*0.19 over c ± bw*0.9/r0 in theme 2 alpha fade*0.45; every other kind with text draws centered arc text of the prefix followed by x. The prefix is "→ " for every "t" line, with no condition. For "u" it is "› " and for "e" it is "× ", each only when the line before l (index minus 1) is missing or has a different kind letter, so a wrapped continuation gets none. Every other kind has no prefix. All crawl arc text uses rr, size, the color, weight and tilt; cw is 0 except table rows. rr shrinks by line height(size) times 0.55 when l is just "p", else times 1. Then WG = 0.

The prompt for session i continues the crawl into vb. live means i's platform is available and i is not demo. ps = S0*1.05; track radii ti = r0 - ps*1.4 and to = r0 + ps*0.5; text middle tm = (ti + to)*0.5 - ps*0.1 and prompt text radius tr = arc_mid(tm, c, ps); half angle th = min(hw*0.9, W*0.42/r0) where hw is the sector half width. Draw a one-color band ti to to over c ± th in theme 4 alpha a*0.72 dark or white alpha a*0.75 light; band ti - 1 to ti + 1 theme 2 alpha a*0.55; band to - 1.5 to to + 1.5 theme 2 alpha a*0.9. For live CUR with empty INPUT: centered arc text "› Ask " + platform name + " anything…" at tr, c, ps, theme 3 alpha a*0.8, weight 0, tilt 1, then e = (2c - its end angle) - `sdf_text_w`("› ", ps)/tr. For live CUR with text: centered arc text "› " + INPUT with newlines shown as spaces at tr, c, ps, theme 2 alpha a, weight 1, tilt 1, and e is its end angle. Live CUR then draws a caret spoke at angle e from tm - ps*0.57 to tm + ps*0.7, width 2.5, theme 2 alpha a*(0.55 + 0.45*cos(NOW*5.5)). Other live sessions draw centered "› " at tr, c, ps, theme 2 alpha a weight 1 tilt 1; sessions that are not live draw centered status(i) at radius arc_mid(tm, c, S0*0.9) and size S0*0.9 in their tone color alpha a, weight 0, tilt 1.

Rim of a sector at c, half width hw, platform q, flags on and busy, into vs: bw = H*0.05; gold (1,0.82,0.45) dark or (0.72,0.52,0.16) light; all bands span c-hw to c+hw. 12 one-color bands R-(k+1)*3 to R-k*3 gold alpha (0.22 dark, 0.12 light)*(1-k/12)*(1-k/12). Bezel: 7 bands k from R+bw*k/7 to R+bw*(k+1)/7 with u = (k+0.5)/7, v = 1 - |2u-1|, color mix of (0.10,0.12,0.17) and (0.27,0.30,0.37) by v*0.8 + 0.2*(1-u) when dark, or of (0.80,0.74,0.62) and (0.97,0.94,0.87) when light, alpha 0.97. Band R+bw*0.58 to R+bw*0.9 platform color alpha 0.33 when on else 0.2. Band R+1 to R+bw*0.22 white alpha 0.07 dark or 0.3 light. Band R-1 to R+1.5 gold alpha 1; band R+bw*0.5-0.5 to R+bw*0.5+0.5 gold 0.25; band R+bw-1 to R+bw+1 gold 0.75. 7 bands R+bw+k*3 to R+bw+(k+1)*3 black alpha (0.35 dark, 0.08 light)*(1-k/7). Sheen: t = NOW, sc = c-hw + (t*0.15 - floor(t*0.15))*2*hw; for k below 15, d = (k-7)/7, a0 = sc + d*0.035, band R to R+bw over a0 to a0+0.0048 color (1,0.97,0.88) alpha 0.22*(1-d*d). Ticks: tk = 0.0087, a from c-hw - (c-hw)%tk while below c+hw stepping tk; big when |a/tk - floor(a/tk/5)*5| is below 0.5; spoke from R+2 to R+bw*0.32 (big) or R+bw*0.2, width 1, gold alpha 0.5 or 0.28. Label: platform name in upper case with a thin space (U+2009) after every letter but the last, then "   ·   ", the rank shown, " / ", cnt(q); size ls = S0*0.62, centered arc text at arc_mid(R + bw*0.5, c, ls), color (1,0.97,0.9) dark or theme 1 light, alpha 1, weight 1, tilt 1; the rank shown is rank(CUR)+1 when on or CUR's platform is q, else 1. When busy, a comet: head = c - hw + (NOW*0.23 - floor(NOW*0.23))*2*hw; for k below 14 a disc at pt(R, head - k*0.0035) of radius 3.5*(1-k/14)+0.8, color (1,0.93,0.75) alpha (1-k/14)*(1-k/14).

Platform tab geometry for q: tab width 172, x0 = W - 172 - 24, y = 18 + q*38, height 30, skew 7; the plus zone is the rightmost 30 pixels. Arrow buttons sit at x 44 and W-44, y = H*0.55.

Keycap legend at (x, y) into vs, for pairs ("← →","session"), ("1–4","platform"), ("+","new"), ("Ctrl T","theme"), ("↑ ↓","scroll"), ("Ctrl V","paste"), ("Enter","send"): w = `sdf_text_w`(key, 9) + 10; rect (x, y, w, 15) theme 2 alpha 0.45, rect (x+1, y+1, w-2, 13) theme 4 alpha 0.9; flat key at (x+5, y+3.5) size 9 theme 1 alpha 0.9 weight 1; flat label at (x+w+5, y+3.5) size 9 theme 3 alpha 0.85; x grows by w + 5 + label width + 13.

The HUD into vs. Logo vertices copied with each position mapped to (20+20+x*20, 18+20+y*20). Flat "A M N I   D I A L" with every plain space between letters a thin space (U+2009) at (70, 20) size 15 theme 2 alpha 1 weight 1. Status dot: tone of CUR; pulse = 0.55+0.45*sin(NOW*4) when busy else 1; disc at (75, 49) radius 7 tone alpha 0.18*pulse, disc radius 3.5 tone alpha pulse; flat status(CUR) at (85, 44) size 10.5 theme 1 alpha 0.85. Path line at (70, 62) size 9 theme 3 alpha 0.8: tilde form of CUR's cwd, or of its directory when the cwd is empty, shortened when longer than 48 bytes to "…/" plus its last three slash-separated parts, then "  ·  session " and the first 8 bytes of its id when the id is non-empty, then "  ·  " and its model when non-empty. Legend at (20, 84). Arrow buttons for s 0 and 1 with direction d = -1 then 1 at their spot (ax, ay): for k below 5 a disc radius 30-k*2 theme 2 alpha 0.04; disc 23 theme 2 alpha 0.75; disc 21.5 theme 4 alpha 0.92 dark or 1 light; segments of width 3 theme 2 alpha 1 from (ax+d*4, ay) to (ax-d*4, ay-8) and from (ax+d*4, ay) to (ax-d*4, ay+8). Platform tabs, on when q is CUR's platform, with corners (x0+7, y), (x0+179, y), (x0+172, y+30), (x0, y+30): on draws the flat quad expanded by 1.5 in theme 2 alpha 1 then the quad in theme 2 alpha 0.95; off draws the expanded quad in theme 2 alpha 0.3 then the quad in theme 4 alpha 0.78 dark or 0.96 light. A stripe quad (x0+7, y), (x0+11, y), (x0+4, y+30), (x0, y+30) in platform color alpha 1. Flat q+1 at (x0+16, y+10) size 10.5 weight 1 and the name at (x0+31, y+10) size 10.5 weight 1, both theme 0 alpha 1 when on, else theme 1 alpha 1 when available or 0.45; flat "+" at (x0+152, y+8) size 12 weight 1, theme 0 when on else theme 2. For each k below cnt(q), with j = nth(q, k): a disc at (x0-12-k*10, y+15), radius 3.5 when j is CUR else 2.3, accent 4 alpha 1 when j is busy, else theme 2 alpha 1 when j is CUR, else theme 2 alpha 0.45.

Drawing to texture out: gpu(); geometry; hw = span*0.5*RAD; rb = R - H*0.8; front = 1.5708; spinning when |ROT-ROT1| exceeds 0.01; NH = 0; vertex lists va, vb and vh. For each session: c = ang(center), d = |wrap((c-front)/RAD)|*RAD; skip when d exceeds hw*2.7; plate: 7 bands k from rb + (R-rb)*k/7 to rb + (R-rb)*(k+1)/7 over c ± hw in theme 4 with inner alpha 0.55*k/7 and outer alpha 0.55*(k+1)/7 when dark, or 0.85 times those when light, times 0.7 when not CUR; then a band R - H*0.25 to R with inner color platform alpha 0 and outer platform alpha 0.07; when CUR or spinning with d below hw*2, the crawl and prompt with alpha 1 for CUR else clamp(1-d/(hw*2), 0, 1); the rim into vb with on = CUR and busy = the session is busy; at both edges e = c-hw then c+hw, two bands into vb that glow at the rim and fade toward the hole: rb to R+H*0.05 over e ± 3.5/R with inner theme 2 alpha 0 and outer theme 2 alpha 0.1, then rb to R+H*0.05 over e ± 0.75/R with inner theme 2 alpha 0 and outer theme 2 alpha 0.7. Then the HUD into vh, so it stays crisp outside the lens effects. Then: hole pass 0; `sdf_draw(SC, W, H, va)`; hole pass 1; `sdf_draw(SC, W, H, vb)`; when DARK: post pass into BL[0] from SC and SC mode 0 strength 1, then into BL[k] from BL[k-1] mode 1 for k 1 to 3, then additive post passes mode 2 strength 1 into BL[k-1] from BL[k] for k from 3 down to 1; finally a post pass into out from SC with glo BL[0], mode 3, strength 0.9 when DARK else 0; last `sdf_draw(out, W, H, vh)`.

Update with dt: when NOW times 4 crosses into a new whole number (compare with a stored last tick) refresh all. u = clamp((NOW-T0)/SPIN, 0, 1) in reals; e = 4u³ below 0.5 else 1 - pow(-2u+2, 3)/2; ROT = ROT0 + (ROT1-ROT0)*e. With n = visible(CUR): if n exceeds CUR's shown, SCROLL = min(SCROLL + (n-shown), 7); shown = n; SCROLL becomes SCROLL*exp(-7*dt).

Click at m: for the arrow buttons, if |m.x-ax| and |m.y-ay| are both below 26, step -1 or 1 and stop. For platform tabs, inside x0 to x0+179 and y to y+30 (half-open): in the plus zone (x at least x0+149) make a session of q and go to it, else go to LASTP[q]; stop.

Typing. Typing codepoint cp appends its UTF-8 bytes to INPUT (1 byte below 128, 2 below 2048, 3 below 65536, else 4). Rubbing out pops bytes from INPUT while the last is a continuation byte (128 to 191), then pops one more, when INPUT is not empty. Pasting appends `gfx::clipboard()` to INPUT dropping "\r" and turning "\n" and "\t" into spaces.

Interactive: `gfx::open("Amni Dial", W, H, gfx::WINDOW_RESIZABLE as int)`, else print "no window: " and `gfx::error()` and stop; `gfx::text_input(true)`; last = `gfx::time()`. While `gfx::frame()`: NOW = `gfx::time()`; W and H from `gfx::screen_size()` x and y; ctrl is `gfx::key_down("Left Ctrl")` or `gfx::key_down("Right Ctrl")`. For each ev in `gfx::events()`: when ev.kind is 2 (text) and not ctrl, with c the ev.codepoint as int: with INPUT empty, c from 49 to 52 goes to LASTP[c-49] and 43 makes a new session of CUR's platform and goes there; else c of at least 32 is typed. When ev.kind is 1 (key), ev.down is set and ev.scancode equals `gfx::scancode("Backspace")` as i32, rub out. Then with `gfx::key_pressed(name)`: "Left" and "Right" step -1 and 1; "Up" or "PageUp" set VIEW = min(VIEW+3, max(0, lines-1)); "Down" or "PageDown" set VIEW = max(0, VIEW-3); "Return" sends; with ctrl, "N" makes a new session of CUR's platform and goes there, "T" toggles DARK and "V" pastes; "Escape" calls `gfx::quit()`. wh = `gfx::mouse_wheel()`; when nonzero VIEW = clamp(VIEW + int(wh*2), 0, max(0, lines-1)). When `gfx::mouse_pressed(1)` click at `gfx::mouse_pos()`. Update with NOW-last, set last = NOW, draw to `gfx::screen()`. `gfx::close()` at the end.

Shots into dir: `mkdir -p '<dir>/frames'`; open headless W by H, else print "no gpu: " + error and stop; an RGBA8 render target. A shot updates by 1/30, draws and saves "dir/name". Filming n frames: each adds 1/30 to NOW and updates by 1/30; when FRAMES is set it also draws, saves "dir/frames/f" + FR zero-padded to 4 digits + ".png", grows FR by 1 and flushes. If OpenCode is available: for k below 3 use nth(3,k) if k is below cnt(3) else make one; refresh; if it has no lines, CUR = it, INPUT = ask k, send. Asks: "In 7 short lines: what makes a polar UI readable?", "Write a 12 line Helium-style haiku sequence about a spinning dial of agents.", "List 7 terse tips for driving several coding agents at once.". Then up to 240 rounds while any session is busy: refresh all, sleep 500 ms. Then reset all sizes and refresh. cc = nth(1,0); go to cc; ROT = ROT0 = ROT1; T0 = -9; shot "dial-rest.png"; HIDE = min(cc lines, 34); cc shown = visible(cc); SCROLL = 0; film 7; while HIDE is positive decrement it and film 4; film 42; shot "dial-crawl.png"; INPUT = "Refactor the crawl so code blocks keep their indentation"; shot "dial-typing.png"; clear INPUT; VIEW = 21; film 7; shot "dial-history.png"; VIEW = 14; film 7; shot "dial-table.png"; VIEW = 0; go to nth(3,0); film 10; shot "dial-spin.png"; film 21; shot "dial-opencode.png"; step 1, film 28; step 1, film 28; go to LASTP[2], film 28; go to nth(0,0), film 28; go to cc, film 28; DARK off; shot "dial-ivory.png"; DARK on; close.

Main: HOME from env; ROOT is env AMNI_DIAL_HOME when set and non-empty, else HOME + "/.amni-dial". Check availability, scan, build the logo, measure font metrics. Arguments in order, for each index k: "--send" with two more sets ask = clamp(int of next - 1, 0, 3) and INPUT to the one after; "--dark" sets DARK; "--ivory" clears DARK; "--frames" sets FRAMES; "--seed" with one more seeds from it; "--shots" with one more sets the shots dir. Refresh all; CUR = first Claude session; go to it; ROT = ROT1. With an ask: go to LASTP[ask], send, then up to 480 times while CUR is busy sleep 500 ms and refresh; print each line of CUR without its kind byte. Then shots when a dir is given, else interactive when there is no ask.
